cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the article named in the README."
title: "e-RT: code and frozen results for the article 'Sequential randomization tests using e-values for clinical trial monitoring across endpoint types'"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zampieri
    given-names: Fernando G.
    affiliation: "Department of Critical Care Medicine, University of Alberta, Edmonton, Alberta, Canada"
  - family-names: Albuquerque
    given-names: Arthur M.
    affiliation: "Universidade Federal do Rio de Janeiro, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil"
  - family-names: Ramdas
    given-names: Aaditya
    affiliation: "Department of Statistics and Data Science, Carnegie Mellon University, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA"
abstract: >-
  R code and frozen simulation outputs for the e-RT article. e-RT is a
  randomization-based e-value method for continuous monitoring of randomized
  trials, with variants for binary (e-RTb), event-only (e-RTe), and continuous
  (e-RTc) endpoints. The repository holds the three kernels, one script per
  simulation, table, and figure of the article and its Electronic Supplementary
  Material, the frozen tables and figures those scripts produced, and checks
  that compare the numbers quoted in the article with the frozen outputs.
  Patient-level ARMA and FACTT data are not included; they are available from
  BioLINCC.
keywords:
  - e-values
  - e-processes
  - randomization tests
  - sequential analysis
  - anytime-valid inference
  - clinical trial monitoring
  - data safety monitoring boards
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fzampier/ert-methods-paper"
